## Key Insights

- Email achieved the highest conversion rate at 50.18%, making it the most effective channel in terms of converting users.
- Referral and Display Ads also performed well, with conversion rates close to 50%.
- Search Ads recorded the lowest conversion rate at 47.98%, indicating potential opportunities for optimization.
- The conversion rates across most channels are relatively close, suggesting balanced marketing performance.
- No channel significantly outperformed the others, which may indicate that multiple channels contribute effectively to conversions.

## Conclusion

Based on conversion rates, Email is the most effective marketing channel in the dataset, while Search Ads is the least effective. Most channels achieved conversion rates near 50%, indicating fairly consistent performance across marketing channels. Further attribution analysis can help determine the exact contribution of each channel to customer conversions.
